<!--
    kuna `gotosink`: two rewrites of a structured statement list run after the
    other structuring passes.  `L: S1..Sk; goto L;` (or `if (c) goto L;` at
    the end) becomes a `while( true )` (or `do ... while (c)`) around the
    statements, with other jumps to `L` from that loop printing as
    `continue;`; `if (c) goto L; S1..Sk; L:` in one list becomes
    `if (!c) { S1..Sk }`.  A run with a free `break;` or `continue;` is left
    alone.  Default on.  The structurer already sinks most local jumps, so
    the sinking witness (normal_ignoreSectionTok) runs with the four
    tail-duplication passes off, which leaves `if (9 <= v) goto L;` above
    the switch it skips.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", option `gotosink on|off`.

    The bytes are normal_getAtts, little2_updatePosition and
    normal_ignoreSectionTok from lib/xmltok.c
    of expat 2.8.2 (MIT, after ./configure), built by gcc 15.3 at -O2
    -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles -nostdlib with unresolved symbols ignored,
    with their jump tables.  Pass 1 is the default; the ignoreSectionTok passes run on, then off;
    the last pass runs the first two with `option gotosink off`.
-->
